cedrus: allow cache hints on the capture queue

The Dash's decoder (spike-vdec) reads every shown picture with the CPU, to rotate it into the panel's framebuffer.
Capture buffers are mapped uncached by default, where the CPU reads them at about 100 MB/s: copying a 1280x480
picture out took 8-9 ms on each core. With cache hints allowed, userspace can ask for cached MMAP buffers
(V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT at REQBUFS). vb2 keeps them coherent: it prepares a buffer at QBUF, and invalidates it
for the CPU when the engine hands the picture back (in cedrus's interrupt), before it can be dequeued. A request
without the flag gets the same buffers as before.

--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -616,6 +616,7 @@
 	dst_vq->timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_COPY;
 	dst_vq->lock = &ctx->dev->dev_mutex;
 	dst_vq->dev = ctx->dev->dev;
+	dst_vq->allow_cache_hints = 1;	/* cached pictures on request (V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT) */
 
 	return vb2_queue_init(dst_vq);
 }
